# gcc -fanalyzer budgets of their own, for files the gate's raised default
# (analyzer-bb-explosion-factor=50, analyzer-max-enodes-per-program-point=64)
# runs out of memory or time on: these get GCC's own default budget, with
# which each finishes inside the 20 GB cap and the 30-minute timeout. At the
# raised budget each ran out of memory or time, in the run the first
# baseline was made with (web_page_base.cc -O0: in a later run, after it
# had finished before). For the unit tests that run out of memory this
# did not help: launch_app_test ran out of memory at GCC's default budget
# too (the others were not tried); they are listed in
# static-analysis.baseline.
# Format: -O0|-O2 <file> <--param...>
-O0 src/util/bcp47.cc --param=analyzer-bb-explosion-factor=5 --param=analyzer-max-enodes-per-program-point=8
